<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title><%= title %> — <%= appName %></title>
  <%- include('../_style') %>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1><%= title %></h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated <%= updatedAt %></p>

    <p class="meaning">
      Both app stores require this page to exist at a stable address, so it is served by the
      API rather than the website.
    </p>

    <h2>From inside the app</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="meaning" style="margin-top:0">
        Open <strong>Settings</strong>, then <strong>Account</strong>, then
        <strong>Delete account</strong>. You will be asked to confirm once.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>What is deleted</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      Your profile, your chanting and sadhana history, your tasks, the struggles you reported,
      your favourites, your reading progress, your notifications and your devices. This is
      immediate and cannot be undone.
    </p>

    <h2>What is kept</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      Records of payments, without your profile attached, for as long as tax and accounting
      rules require. Nothing in them identifies you to anyone reading the app.
    </p>

    <h2>If you cannot reach the app</h2>
    <p class="meaning">
      Email <a href="mailto:support@hariharibol.com">support@hariharibol.com</a> from the
      address on the account and we will delete it for you.
    </p>

    <footer class="muted"><p><%= appName %> &middot; <%= year %></p></footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
